{"nodes": [{"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_encoder_menu", "label": "Menu of Disease-Agnostic Shared Spatio-Temporal Encoders", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eight encoder families assessed against three architectural filters derived from the seven hard constraints."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_option1_inductive_tcn_gnn", "label": "Option 1: Inductive Temporal-Per-Node Encoder Plus Inductive Spatial Message Passing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recommended first: the only family size-agnostic by construction, needing no node identities, with a small trunk friendly to MAML and adapters; cost is some in-distribution accuracy versus adaptive-graph models, which is the price of transferability."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_option2_stgcn_gated_tcn", "label": "Option 2: STGCN-Style GCN Plus Gated TCN", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recommended second as the efficient fully-inductive comparator; limited to a predefined graph, which is acceptable because latent-graph learning is what breaks transfer."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_option3_dcrnn", "label": "Option 3: DCRNN-Style Diffusion Plus Recurrence", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Conditional: the core operator is inductive but the autoregressive seq2seq decoder conflicts with direct multi-horizon and recurrent rollout is slow at 7,165 nodes on 8 GB."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_option4_adaptive_graph_stgnn", "label": "Option 4: Adaptive-Graph STGNNs (REJECT for shared trunk)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Learned node embeddings are transductive, indexed by node and sized by N, so weights cannot move across graph sizes and would encode disease identity; the gated dilated TCN and diffusion conv minus the adaptive term are salvageable."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_option5_epidemic_gnns", "label": "Option 5: Epidemic-Specific GNNs (REJECT trunk, borrow motifs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EpiGNN is provably size-locked via a learnable NxN matrix; mechanistic-prior models bake in disease-specific compartmental parameters that violate disease-agnosticism. Cola-GNN's location-aware attention and EpiGNN's multi-scale temporal convolutions are transferable motifs."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_option6_st_transformers", "label": "Option 6: Spatio-Temporal Transformers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Attention can be made inductive and GMAN's transform-attention decoder fits direct multi-horizon, but O(TN^2)/O(NT^2) cost is prohibitive at 7,165 nodes on 8 GB; viable only for the 10-61 node graphs."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_option7_foundation_models", "label": "Option 7: Pre-Trained ST and Time-Series Foundation Encoders", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use a small TSFM as the per-node temporal module or a zero-shot baseline, but do not adopt a large frozen foundation model as the whole trunk: 8 GB, SHAP transparency and few-shot inner loops all argue against it."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_option8_cape_pems", "label": "Option 8: Epidemic Pre-Trained Temporal Models (CAPE / PEMS)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Closest prior art: they prove cross-disease pre-training works but are purely temporal with no spatial encoder, which is the exact gap this project fills. Treat as must-cite baselines and a pre-training template."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_filter_a_size_agnostic", "label": "Filter A: No Node Identities, Size-Agnostic", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shared weights may not contain any parameter indexed by node or sized by N, which immediately disqualifies transductive adaptive-graph learners."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_filter_b_direct_multi_horizon", "label": "Filter B: Direct Multi-Horizon, Factorisable, Cheap at 7,165 Nodes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Favours factorised temporal-then-spatial designs with a direct multi-head output and penalises O(N^2) dense spatial attention or per-node recurrence at dengue scale."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_filter_c_meta_conformal_shap", "label": "Filter C: Few-Shot, Conformal and SHAP Friendliness", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Favours a small shared trunk with a light adaptation surface, stable latent features, and no reliance on a held-out calibration split."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_transductive_node_embeddings", "label": "Transductive Node Embeddings as a Disqualifying Pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Parameters indexed by node hard-wire a fixed node count and leak disease identity; inductivity comes from parameter-sharing over local neighbourhoods, not from node lookups."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_online_aci", "label": "Online Adaptive Conformal Inference", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Needs no held-out calibration set and wraps any forecaster, which suits a project whose target disease carries no calibration split; feature-space online conformal is easiest on a small stable trunk."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_shap_on_latent", "label": "SHAP Attribution on the Latent", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cleanest on a low-dimensional stable latent, expensive and unstable on large attention stacks and opaque on frozen foundation models."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_size_transferability_theory", "label": "GNN Size-Transferability Theory (Graphons and Graphops)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supports carry-over across differently sized graphs when the local operator is shared, but the guarantees are asymptotic and assume structurally similar graphs, so a 10 to 7,165 node range must be validated not assumed."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_cape", "label": "CAPE (arXiv:2502.03393)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_pems", "label": "PEMS (Kamarthi and Prakash, ICLR 2024)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_graph_wavenet", "label": "Graph WaveNet (Wu et al., IJCAI 2019)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_mtgnn", "label": "MTGNN", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_agcrn", "label": "AGCRN (Bai et al., NeurIPS 2020)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "progress_decisions_encoder_decision_epignn", "label": "EpiGNN (Xie et al., PRICAI 2022)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Encoder Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "ca